# skill-hint synonym map — RU → EN
#
# Each line: <lowercase stem>  <english terms the skill descriptions actually use…>
# A stem found anywhere in the prompt appends its terms to the text the hook tokenizes.
# Stems are raw substrings, so write the shortest unambiguous root: "эпик" catches
# "эпика"/"эпику"/"эпиком". Lines starting with # and lines with <2 fields are ignored.
# **Separate the stem from its terms with 2+ spaces.** That run of spaces is the delimiter, so a
# stem may contain single spaces ("не публик"); one space between stem and terms still works for
# single-token stems, but a multi-word stem written that way truncates to its first token.
#
# Rule of thumb when adding: the right-hand terms must appear in some SKILL.md `name:`,
# `description:` or `when_to_use:` — the hook scores against those three, nothing else.
# Terms shorter than 4 chars are dropped by the tokenizer, so write "docs" not "doc".

# --- epics, plans, backlog ------------------------------------------------
эпик        epic backlog
закрыт      close closing epic terminal
закрой      close closing epic
карточк     card backlog plan
бэклог      backlog epic
план        plan planning prepare decompose
подготов    prepare analysis plan
декомпоз    decompose subtask atomic parallel
разб        decompose subtask breakdown parallel
статус      status dashboard progress
сводк       status dashboard summary
волн        wave backlog
реализ      implement implementation subtask
# закрытие эпика: «реализовал X, проверь всё ли сделано, можно в realised?» — самый частый
# неуправляемый шаблон в корпусе (7 из 17 ложных срабатываний /triage). Всё это /close-epic.
реализовал  implemented done verify closing terminal
реализовали implemented done verify closing terminal
завершил    done closing terminal realised verify
выполнен    done closing terminal verify
перенест    realised closing terminal done
перенос     realised closing terminal done
готово      done closing terminal verify
внедр       implement implementation

